{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QouExistsAxiom3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QouExistsAxiom3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_axiom_3_chern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_axiom_3_chern","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-exists-axiom-3.lean#L32-L45","doc":"**Axiom 3 — Chern-class vanishing (categorical form).**\n\nAny `QuantumObservableUniverse R` carries the `adjoint_vanishing`\nfield, asserting that all morphisms `𝟙 → Ad(A)` in `C` agree —\nthe `Subsingleton` form of \"no non-trivial invariant adjoint\nmorphisms\".  This is the categorical analogue of vanishing\nChern classes for the adjoint bundle. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:qou-exists-axiom-3","label":"lem:qou-exists-axiom-3","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-exists-axiom-3.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}